# --- macOS / IDE / local env ---
.DS_Store
.idea/
.venv/
# Agent/tooling scratch directories. Machine-local, not part of the product.
/.claude/
/.superpowers/
# MCP server config — points at a per-session localhost port (e.g. the
# PyCharm bridge), so it is machine-specific and useless to teammates.
.mcp.json

# --- Local-only material (delivered out-of-band, never pushed) ---
# CLAUDE.md is the maintainer's working notebook (release narrative, bug
# history, open issues). SECURITY_ASSESSMENT.md enumerates where real secrets
# live. Neither belongs in a public repo. PDFs are generated artifacts; the
# .md sources are authoritative.
/CLAUDE.md
/SECURITY_ASSESSMENT.md
*.pdf
# Narrowed from a blanket /docs/ so the operator-facing guides can be tracked.
# Only maintainer-private subtrees stay ignored; anything local-only added to
# docs/ later needs its own rule here.
/docs/superpowers/
/docs/claude/
/docs/n8n-seed-scratch.md
# These two document working default credentials -- a login password and a
# PoolParty superadmin pair one of them states the deployment requires
# verbatim. They stay on disk and are distributed out-of-band. Anything
# referencing them from a tracked doc must not link to them.
/docs/QUICK-START.md
/docs/STACK-DEPLOYMENT.md
/n8n/
/n8n-workflows/
/files/

# --- Secrets (exact-name; *.example variants stay tracked) ---
**/graphwise-secrets.yaml
**/terraform.tfvars
**/n8n.txt

# --- Terraform run artifacts, anywhere ---
**/.terraform/
**/.terraform.lock.hcl
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
crash.log

# --- License blobs (depth-agnostic; survives a parent-dir rename) ---
**/licenses/*
!**/licenses/README.txt

# --- Helm nested-subchart tarballs / lockfiles (silent-stale-tarball footgun) ---
**/Chart.lock
**/charts/*.tgz
# ...except the umbrella's own vendored deps, which ARE committed intentionally
!charts/graphwise-stack/charts/*.tgz

# --- workflow Postgres dumps: NEVER committed anywhere in the repo. The seed
#     lives only on the EC2 home root as a FREEFORM-named $HOME/workflows*.sql
#     (e.g. workflows-acme-demo.sql, or the auto-named workflows-pg-dumpall-<date>.sql)
#     -- scp'd up by the operator or made by create-workflows-dumpall.sh;
#     restore-workflows-dumpall.sh loads the newest by mtime. The broad
#     **/workflows*.sql glob keeps any use-case-named seed from leaking, no matter
#     the wildcard portion (see the license-leak-on-rename lesson in CLAUDE.md). ---
**/workflows*.sql
**/n8n-pg-dumpall*.sql

# --- Ontotext Refine: not shipped ---
#     Dropped at 3.0.0. The chart still carries a refine subchart, disabled by
#     default, that an amd64 operator can enable against the upstream
#     `ontotext/refine` image. The arm64 local-build path (a vendor dist under
#     refine/, plus infra/refine-image/) is not part of the release.
/refine/
/infra/refine-image/

# local kubectl/command scratchpad (never commit)
/foo

# Nested agent settings. The root-anchored /.claude/ above does not match
# these; the laptop kit carries one at terraform-aws/.claude/.
**/.claude/settings.local.json

# Operator's master copy of files/, kept outside the module.
/files.master/

# n8n pg_dumpall output, whatever it gets named.
**/*n8n*dump*.sql
